            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "text": "The authors use stabilizer-work monotonicity and subadditivity to give necessary bounds for exact finite-copy conversion, T-state cost and distillation, and claim that crossing work curves rule out conversion in both directions. They explicitly state that work-curve dominance is not sufficient for conversion. This is an unverified author-claim candidate."
      }
